=== Hall of Mirror Clones ===
*Clone HitPtr copies the Main HitPtr.
*Not affected by Extra Hits.

=== Extra Hits ===
Sources of [[Extra Hit]] include:
*{{A|Xata's Whisper}} - adds one independent HitPtr with {{D|Void}} Damage
*{{A|Toxic Lash}} - adds one independent HitPtr with {{D|Toxin}} Damage
*{{A|Resupply}} - adds one independent HitPtr with Elemental Damage
*{{A|Silken Stride}} - adds one independent HitPtr with {{D|Toxin}} Damage
*{{Arcane|Melee Duplicate}} - on basic [[Critical Hit]], it has a chance to add one independent HitPtr that copies the DmgSrcs of the hit that procced it

=== Distribution Hits ===
"Distribution Hits" comes from effects that distribute the damage instantly to multiple targets from the avatar's original hit.

Sources of Distribution Hit include:
*{{A|Tornado}} - adds up to 3 HitPtrs based on the number of hits; adds HitPtrs by copying and distributing the DmgSrcs of the HitPtrs it hits.
*{{M|Funnel Clouds}} - adds up to 8 HitPtrs based on the number of hits; adds HitPtrs by copying and distributing the DmgSrcs of the HitPtrs it hits.

=== Status Hits ===
{{UpdateMe|Clarification needed, is the guaranteed proc from {{A|Resupply}} associated with the Extra HitPtr?
*Resupply does not appear to be strongly related to Extra HitPtr. The guaranteed 100% Status Effect proc clearly seems to use the same underlying implementation as Silken Stride, as this “guaranteed Status proc” behavior already appears to be built into this template at the code level.}}

Status HitPtrs comes from [[Status Effect]]s that proc on hitting enemies with a Main HitPtr or Other HitPtr.
* Status HitPtrs cannot proc additional status effects.
* Status HitPtrs and OtherPtrs apply on different timelines and need to be calculated independently.
* Each HitStruct can have only one DoT HitPtr of the same condition.
** For example, if a weapon procs both {{D|Heat}} and {{D|Toxin}} on two projectiles that hit the enemy at the same time, then one HitStruct will have {{D|Heat}} DoT HitPtrs and the other HitStruct will have {{D|Toxin}} DoT HitPtrs.
* Each HitStruct can have at most as many Blast Proc HitPtrs as the enemy's Blast stack limit.

Sources of Status Hits include:
*Status AoE Damage HitPtr - {{D|Blast}}, resolves and causes AoE damage to hit enemies
*DoT HitPtr (DoTPtr) - each HitStruct can have only one DoT damage of the same condition type

Notes:
* Status AoE Damage HitPtr refers to {{D|Blast}} procs; upon resolution, each stack causes AoE damage to enemies, and each stack counts as one HitPtr.
* Each HitStruct can have at most as many Status AoE Damage HitPtrs as the current maximum stacks on the enemy.
* Each HitStruct can have only one DoT HitPtr of the same condition type.
* Each HitStruct can have at most as many Blast HitPtrs as the enemy's Blast stack limit.
* In Status HitPtr, within a single HitStruct, Slash DoTs merge into one DmgSrc regardless of how many DmgSrcs there are.
* {{A|Resupply}} cannot attach an independent DoTPtr for elements (clarification needed, is the guaranteed proc is associated with the Extra HitPtr?).
* {{D|Heat}} DoT can only have one HitPtr due to its unique [[Heat Inherit]] mechanic.
* {{D|Electricity}} DoT can only have one HitPtr due to its unique [[Electricity Damage|Tesla Chain]] mechanic.
* {{D|Gas}} DoT can only have one HitPtr due to its unique [[Gas Damage|Gas Clouds]] mechanic.

=== Rebound and Bouncing Hits ===
* If MainPtrs [[bounce]] off a surface and hit an enemy again, a ReboundPtr will be created.
** MainPtrs include: weapon's MainPtrs and {{A|Hall of Mirrors}} ClonePtrs.
* ReboundPtr counts as a MainPtr; most ReboundPtr hit timings almost never overlap with other MainPtr hit timings.
* ReboundPtr inherits the [[Extra Hit]] bonuses of its MainPtr.
** For example, with {{A|Xata's Whisper}} active, firing {{Weapon|Cyanex}} once: MainPtr has 1 AoE HitPtr and 1 Projectile HitPtr; AddPtrs are 2 Xata's Whisper HitPtrs. When that hits an enemy and bounces to hit again, it will again deal 1 AoE HitPtr and 1 Projectile HitPtr plus 2 Xata's Whisper HitPtrs.
* ClonePtr cannot have Extra Hits; so clone-generated ReboundPtrs can calculate HitPtr counts based on Distribution Hit effects.
* Because ReboundPtr is on a different timeline than OtherPtrs and MainPtrs, a ReboundPtr count formula cannot be derived.


== HitPtr Count Formulas ==
*Note: if an effect that increases HitPtr is active, set as 1; if not, set as 0. Thus, they appear as (0~1) in the formulas.

=== Single Main Hit Count Formula ===
<math>{
\text{Single MainPtr Count} = 1
}</math>

=== Extra Hit Count Formula ===
<math>
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total Extra Hit Count} &=\text{Single MainPtr Count} \times (\text{Xata's Whisper} + \text{Toxic Lash} + \text{Resupply} + \text{Silken Stride} + \text{Melee Duplicate}) \\
&= 1 \times \big[ (0 \sim 1) + (0 \sim 1) + (0 \sim 1) + (0 \sim 1) + (0 \sim 1) \big]
\end{aligned}
</math>

=== Distribution Hit Count Formula ===
* Each {{A|Tornado}} counts as one Distribution Hit HitPtr, up to 3 Tornados.
* Each {{M|Funnel Clouds|Funnel Cloud}} counts as one Distribution Hit HitPtr, up to 8 Tornados.

<math>{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total Distribution Hit Count} &= \text{Single MainPtr Count} \times (\text{Number of Tornados Hit} + \text{Number of Funnel Clouds Tornados Hit}) \\
&= 1 \times \big[ (0 \sim 3) + (0 \sim 8) \big]
\end{aligned}
}</math>

=== Clone Hit Count Formula === 
* {{A|Hall of Mirrors}} clone attacks cannot have HitPtrs added by Extra Hit effects but can increase HitPtrs by hitting enemies with Distribution Hit abilities like {{A|Tornado}}. 
* Each clone's attack replicates that attack's MainPtr, so clones have their own MainPtr counted as ClonePtr.
* To calculate the number of ClonePtrs, determine how many clones exist, whether each clone hit the enemy, and how many Distribution Hit HitPtrs each Clone Hit produced. 

'''Clone Hit count for one clone formula:''' 

<math>{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total nth Clone Hit Count} &= \text{Is there an nth Clone?} \times \text{Did that nth Clone hit the enemy?} \\
&= 1 \times (0 \sim 1)
\end{aligned}
}</math>

<hr />

'''Number of Distribution Hits that were hit by a single Clone Hit formula:''' 

<math>{ 
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total nth Clone Hit and Distribution Hit Count} &= \text{Is there an nth Clone?} + \text{Did that nth Clone hit a Tornado?} \times (\text{Number of Tornados the nth Clone hit} + \text{Did the nth Clone hit Funnel Clouds?}) \\
&= (0 \sim 1) + \big[ (0 \sim 1) \times \big[ (1 \sim 0) \times [ (1 \sim 3) + (0 \sim 8) ] \big] \big]
\end{aligned}
}</math>

<hr />

* Note: These {{A|Hall of Mirrors}} clone formulas depend on a single MainPtr of the current weapon.
* Up to 6 clones, so each ClonePtr's replicated single MainPtr's final HitPtr count must be calculated according to the actual situation.
** For example, {{Weapon|Kuva Quartakk}} Burst-Fire While Aiming has 4 MainPtrs hit in one attack; the Clone Hit and Distribution Hit Count formula can only calculate one MainPtr from the 4 MainPtrs in each replicated attack per clone.
*** {{Weapon|Kuva Quartakk}} is cloned by Hall Of Mirrors into 2 clones; each clone fires 4 ClonePtrs, so that one Burst-Fire While Aiming attack requires calculating the Clone Hit and Distribution Hit Count 8 times to determine how many HitPtrs Hall Of Mirrors added.

=== Single MainPtr Final Hit Count Formula ===
* Each weapon's main attack needs its own calculation of how many MainPtrs appear.
** For example, projectile attacks, melee attacks, and other AoE attacks must be calculated separately.
** For example, {{Weapon|Stropha}}'s attack: maintaining very close range to the enemy and attacking produces one melee attack and one projectile attack, which is 2 MainPtrs. If multiple HitPtr increasing effects are used, each MainPtr's final HitPtr count must be calculated independently.
* Note: Each MainPtr must use the formula below to calculate its final HitPtr count.
** For example, {{Weapon|Kuva Quartakk}} Burst-Fire While Aiming has 4 MainPtrs; each of these 4 MainPtrs must be calculated separately using the formula below, then summed to get the total HitPtrs.

<hr />

<math>{ 
\begin{aligned}
\text{Single MainPtr Final Hit Count} ={}&
\text{Single MainPtr Count} \\
&+ \text{Total Extra Hit Count} \\
&+ \text{Total Distribution Hit Count} \\
&+ \text{Total First Clone Hit Count} \\
&+ \text{Total Second Clone Hit Count} \\
&+ \text{Total Third Clone Hit Count} \\
&+ \text{Total Fourth Clone Hit Count} \\
&+ \text{Total Fifth Clone Hit Count} \\
&+ \text{Total Sixth Clone Hit Count} \\
\end{aligned}
}</math> 

<math>{ 
\begin{aligned}
\text{Single MainPtr Final Hit Count} ={}&
(1) \\
&+ (1 \times \big[ (0\sim1) + (0\sim1) + (0\sim1) + (0 \sim 1) + (0\sim1)) \big] \\
&+ (1 \times (1\sim3 + (0\sim1))) + \\
&+ (1\sim0 + (1\sim0 \times (1\sim3 + (0\sim8)))) \\
&+ (1\sim0 + (1\sim0 \times (1\sim3 + (0\sim8)))) \\
&+ (1\sim0 + (1\sim0 \times (1\sim3 + (0\sim8)))) \\
&+ (1\sim0 + (1\sim0 \times (1\sim3 + (0\sim8)))) \\
&+ (1\sim0 + (1\sim0 \times (1\sim3 + (0\sim8)))) \\
&+ (1\sim0 + (1\sim0 \times (1\sim3 + (0\sim8)))) \\   
\end{aligned}
}</math>

<hr />

Notes:
* Each weapon's MainPtr must calculate HitPtrs independently.
** For example, {{Weapon|Sampotes}}' Heavy Slam Attack wave, {{Weapon|Tenet Exec}}'s Heavy Attack wave.
*** {{Weapon|Sampotes}} Heavy Slam Attack has 13 MainPtrs; each slam wave must independently calculate HitPtr count.
* Multiple additional AoE attacks that increase HitPtrs can only be DmgSrcs and cannot calculate HitPtrs independently.

=== Status Hit HitPtr Formula ===
[[Status Effect|DoT]]-type HitPtr count is determined by the number of HitStructs.
* For example, two different HitStructs trigger SlashCondition ({{D|Slash}} proc), ToxicCondition ({{D|Toxin}} proc), ShockCondition ({{D|Electricity}} proc), HeatCondition ({{D|Heat}} proc), and GasCondition ({{D|Gas}} proc). Regardless of how many DmgSrcs caused these procs or how many proc stacks:
**The GasCondition can only have a maximum of 10 GasConditionDoT.
**The SlashCondition, ShockCondition, and ToxicCondition can only have a maximum of 2 DoTPtr of the same type of status effect because there are only 2 HitStructs.
**The HeatCondition can only be 1 HeatConditionDotPtr because of its unique [[Heat Inherit]] mechanic. The same applies to [[Electricity]] and [[Gas]].
* Within the same HitStruct, Slash DoT will merge into a single DmgSrc. The same applies to Toxic DoT.
* {{D|Heat}} DoT can only have one HitPtr due to its unique [[Heat Inherit]] mechanic.
* {{D|Electricity}} DoT can only have one HitPtr due to its unique [[Electricity Damage|Tesla Chain]] mechanic.
* {{D|Gas}} DoT can only have one HitPtr due to its unique [[Gas Damage|Gas Clouds]] mechanic.
====Blast Proc Hit Count Formula====
<math>{
\text{Total Blast Procs Hit Count} = \text{Blast Proc Stack Count} + \text{Resupply's Blast Proc Stack Count}
}</math>

====Damage Over Time Hit Count Formula====
<math>{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total nth HitStruct DoT Hit Count} ={}& 
\text{Does this nth HitStruct have Slash proc?} \\
&+ \text{Does this nth HitStruct have Toxin proc?} 
\end{aligned}
}</math>

<math>{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total nth HitStruct DoT Hit Count} ={}& 
n \times ( 0\sim 1 ) \\
&+ n \times ( 0\sim 1 )
\end{aligned}
}</math>

====Heat Proc Hit Count Formula====
<math>{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total Heat DoT Hit Count} &= 1 \times \text{Does the enemy have Heat proc?} \\
&= 1 \times (0 \sim 1)
\end{aligned}
}</math>

====Electricity Proc Hit Count Formula====
<math>{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total Heat DoT Hit Count} &= 1 \times \text{Does the enemy have Electricity proc?} \\
&= 1 \times (0 \sim 1)
\end{aligned}
}</math>

====Gas Proc Hit Count Formula====
<math>{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Total Heat DoT Hit Count} &= 1 \times \text{Does the enemy have Gas proc?} \\
&= 1 \times (0 \sim 1)
\end{aligned}
}</math>

== Summary ==
* {{A|Xata's Whisper}}, {{A|Toxic Lash}}, {{A|Resupply}}, and {{Arcane|Melee Duplicate}} each count as 1 in HitPtr calculations.
* {{A|Tornado}} counts as 1-3 in HitPtr calculations.
* {{M|Funnel Clouds}} counts as 1-8 in HitPtr calculations.
* {{A|Hall of Mirrors}} clones count as 0-6 clones based on actual number (some weapons like {{Weapon|Syam}}'s Heavy Attack can use 6 clones to attack).
* {{D|Blast}} proc resolution counts as the number of stacks at resolution time for Status Hit HitPtr, with {{A|Resupply}}'s Status Hit being separate.
* {{A|Hall of Mirrors}} will clone 0 to 6 Warframe clones that follow the main Warframe's attacks from different positions depending on weapon, making hit counts variable.
* AoE attack and projectile attack HitPtrs are different MainPtrs and must be calculated separately.
* Each attack hit's HitPtr count must be calculated independently (i.e., attacks hitting at different times).
* Status proc calculations must be separate because those formulas operate on the HitStruct timeline, not the others.
* For each weapon, each attack counts as 1 MainPtr. For example, {{Weapon|Kronen}} performing two Heavy Attacks counts as 4 MainPtrs.
* Each HitStruct can have only one HitPtr of the same Status Effect type.
* In the HitStruct, the {{D|Slash}} DoT in the DoT HitPtr will, combine all the DmgSrcs of {{D|Slash}} DoT into a single DmgSrc if they are within the same HitStruct, regardless of the number of DmgSrcs.

